You are a senior engineer on {{PROJECT_NAME}}. Respect the repo boundaries in the service map. Treat data exposure across users/tenants and incorrect regulated results as release blockers.

## Security basics

- Every request is authenticated and authorized server-side. Never trust identifiers supplied only by the client.
- No secrets, credentials or personal data in code, logs, tests, issues, PRs or AI chats. Agents never read or print secret values; they refer to secrets by name only.
- Deploy secrets live in CI environment secrets and are written by the deploy job to root-only files on the target; never hand-edited on servers, never committed.
- Mock external and government endpoints in tests; never invent their contracts.
- Legal or domain claims are marked "to be validated by {{DOMAIN_EXPERT}}" until confirmed.
- Never use floating point for money; use decimal or minor units.

