## Environments and releases

- Staging: {{STAGING_URL}} — deploys from pull requests and `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` after checks pass.
- Production: {{PROD_URL}} — only via a manual, human-approved release workflow. Nothing deploys to production automatically.
- `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` changes only through pull requests. Image build/deploy jobs run only when lint, test and security jobs pass in the same run.
- Before a release, verify `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` contains every reviewed commit of the released PRs (`docs/agents/release-checklist.md`).

## How to route work

- Which repo owns what, interfaces, routing table and change order: `{{DOCS_REPO}}/docs/architecture/service-map.md`.
- Agents and skills cheat sheet: `docs/agents/how-to-use-agents.md`.
- Vague request → `task-intake` skill; multi-repo ticket → `cross-repo-feature` skill. Skills live in `.agents/skills/` (read by OpenCode and VS Code Copilot).
- Ticket readiness and labels: `docs/agents/ticket-standard.md`; issue forms in `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`.
- Agents: single source in `agents/<name>.md`; run `python3 scripts/sync-agents.py` to generate `.opencode/agents/` and `.github/agents/` and commit both. Never edit generated files; CI runs `--check`.
- Flow: implementer → `test-engineer` → `security-reviewer` (+ `domain-reviewer`) → human merge. Reviewers are read-only. PRs touching auth, sessions or crypto are reviewed twice (initial and after fixes).

## Definition of done: documentation (mandatory for every agent and engineer)

Work is not finished until the documentation matches it. In the same PR (or a linked `{{DOCS_REPO}}` PR):

- Update `README.md` / `CONTRIBUTING.md` when setup, commands, layout, environment variables or behaviour change.
- Record any architectural or cross-repo decision as an ADR in `{{DOCS_REPO}}/docs/adr/`; update an existing ADR's status if superseded.
- Update `{{DOCS_REPO}}` when infrastructure, deployment, security, data access or release flow change.
- Add or correct terms in `{{DOCS_REPO}}/GLOSSARY.md` when new domain terms appear.
- Comment on the related GitHub issue (what changed, links, follow-ups); open new issues for deferred work instead of leaving TODOs.
- The final report of every agent lists which docs were updated, or states why none were needed.
